---
import '../styles/global.css';

/*
 * TEMPORARY REVIEW PAGE. Not part of the route map in design.md section 2.1,
 * not linked from Header, noindex. Built to compare real CSS options for the
 * five weak points the leader flagged, side by side, so a choice can be made
 * before anything touches the live sections. Delete this file once every
 * section below has a decision.
 */
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Design review, internal only</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <main id="main" class="rev-shell">
      <header class="rev-banner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Internal, not part of the site</p>
        <h1>Timberline visual review</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Five weak points, two or three real options each. Nothing here is
          live on the actual page yet. Say which letter wins per section, or
          keep the baseline, and I will fold only that choice into the real
          component.
        </p>
        <nav class="rev-jump" aria-label="Jump to section">
          <a href="#rev-glow">1. Hero glow</a>
          <a href="#rev-mobile">2. Mobile at 375px</a>
          <a href="#rev-chips">3. Capability chips</a>
          <a href="#rev-stats">4. Stat cards</a>
          <a href="#rev-texture">5. Grain and contours</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- 1. HERO GLOW -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <section class="rev-section" id="rev-glow">
        <h2>1. Hero glow</h2>
        <p class="rev-intro">
          Same badge and headline fragment in all three, only the glow layer
          changes. Judging presence versus smear.
        </p>
        <div class="rev-grid rev-grid-3">
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">A — Baseline, current</p>
            <div class="stage stage-hero grain contours">
              <div class="glow-a" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class="stage-hero-content above">
                <p class="badge">
                  <span class="badge-chip">v4</span>
                  <span>LoRa mesh · Field to basecamp</span>
                </p>
                <h3 class="stage-h1">
                  When the bars run out,<br />
                  <span class="accent">the mesh carries on</span>
                </h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">One wide, soft radial. Reads as ambience, easy to miss on a bright display.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">B — Layered halo</p>
            <div class="stage stage-hero grain contours">
              <div class="glow-a" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class="glow-b-core" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class="glow-b-vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class="stage-hero-content above">
                <p class="badge">
                  <span class="badge-chip">v4</span>
                  <span>LoRa mesh · Field to basecamp</span>
                </p>
                <h3 class="stage-h1">
                  When the bars run out,<br />
                  <span class="accent">the mesh carries on</span>
                </h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              Keeps the wide wash, adds a tighter brighter core behind the badge and a soft
              corner vignette so the glow reads by contrast, not just intensity.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">C — Beam</p>
            <div class="stage stage-hero grain contours">
              <div class="glow-c-beam" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class="glow-c-core" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class="stage-hero-content above">
                <p class="badge">
                  <span class="badge-chip">v4</span>
                  <span>LoRa mesh · Field to basecamp</span>
                </p>
                <h3 class="stage-h1">
                  When the bars run out,<br />
                  <span class="accent">the mesh carries on</span>
                </h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              A directional shaft falling from top centre, like a headlamp cast down the
              page. More editorial, further from the two reference sites.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- 2. MOBILE AT 375PX -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <section class="rev-section" id="rev-mobile">
        <h2>2. Mobile at 375px</h2>
        <p class="rev-intro">
          The stat row and the capability chips are the two spots in the hero with the
          least mobile-specific thought. Frames below are fixed at 375px, the standard
          small-phone width.
        </p>
        <div class="rev-grid rev-grid-2">
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">A — Current behaviour</p>
            <div class="phone-frame">
              <ul class="m-stats m-stats-a">
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">3</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Node versions in the field</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">30 s</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">To cancel a false fall alarm before anything is sent</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">0</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Cell towers required between handsets</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <ul class="m-chips m-chips-a">
                {['LoRa mesh', 'GPS position', 'Fall detection', 'Device SOS broadcast', 'Store and forward', 'Basecamp gateway'].map((c) => (
                  <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>{c}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              Stats stack to three full-height cards, a long scroll before the chips even
              start. Chips centre-wrap into a ragged four-line block.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">B — Compact bento and tape</p>
            <div class="phone-frame">
              <ul class="m-stats m-stats-b">
                <li class="glass stat stat-lead">
                  <span class="stat-value">3</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Node versions in the field</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">30 s</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Cancel window</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">0</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Towers needed</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <div class="m-chips-b-wrap">
                <ul class="m-chips m-chips-b">
                  {['LoRa mesh', 'GPS position', 'Fall detection', 'Device SOS broadcast', 'Store and forward', 'Basecamp gateway'].map((c) => (
                    <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>{c}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              One lead stat spans full width at full size, the other two share a row at a
              reduced label. Chips become one horizontal scroll strip with an edge fade,
              like a spec tape, instead of wrapping.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- 3. CAPABILITY CHIPS -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <section class="rev-section" id="rev-chips">
        <h2>3. Capability chip row</h2>
        <p class="rev-intro">
          Same six capabilities, three treatments. This row is the only place capability
          claims appear as a set, so it can afford to carry more brand.
        </p>
        <div class="rev-grid rev-grid-3">
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">A — Baseline, current</p>
            <div class="stage stage-chips">
              <ul class="chips-a">
                {['LoRa mesh', 'GPS position', 'Fall detection', 'Device SOS broadcast', 'Store and forward', 'Basecamp gateway'].map((c) => (
                  <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>{c}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">Individually bordered pills, near-invisible against the page.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">B — Manifest plate</p>
            <div class="stage stage-chips">
              <ul class="chips-b glass">
                {['LoRa mesh', 'GPS position', 'Fall detection', 'Device SOS broadcast', 'Store and forward', 'Basecamp gateway'].map((c) => (
                  <li><span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>{c}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              The whole row becomes one glass plate, items separated by hairline dividers
              rather than each carrying its own border. Reads as a spec sheet, one object.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">C — Field tags</p>
            <div class="stage stage-chips">
              <ul class="chips-c">
                {['LoRa mesh', 'GPS position', 'Fall detection', 'Device SOS broadcast', 'Store and forward', 'Basecamp gateway'].map((c, i) => (
                  <li><span class="chip-index">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{c}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              Each item gets a brass left edge and a two-digit index, echoing the R&D
              section's numbered cards. No checkmark; the index carries the "included" read.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- 4. STAT CARDS -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <section class="rev-section" id="rev-stats">
        <h2>4. Stat cards</h2>
        <p class="rev-intro">Same three numbers, three card treatments.</p>
        <div class="rev-grid rev-grid-3">
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">A — Baseline, current</p>
            <div class="stage stage-stats">
              <ul class="stats-a">
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">3</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Node versions in the field</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">30 s</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">To cancel a false fall alarm</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat">
                  <span class="stat-value">0</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Cell towers required</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">Flat glass panel, number and label, no other hierarchy device.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">B — Plate and rule</p>
            <div class="stage stage-stats">
              <ul class="stats-b">
                <li class="plate stat-b">
                  <span class="stat-b-eyebrow">Field data</span>
                  <span class="stat-value stat-b-value">3</span>
                  <span class="stat-b-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Node versions in the field</span>
                </li>
                <li class="plate stat-b">
                  <span class="stat-b-eyebrow">Field data</span>
                  <span class="stat-value stat-b-value">30 s</span>
                  <span class="stat-b-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="stat-label">To cancel a false fall alarm</span>
                </li>
                <li class="plate stat-b">
                  <span class="stat-b-eyebrow">Field data</span>
                  <span class="stat-value stat-b-value">0</span>
                  <span class="stat-b-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Cell towers required</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              Neomorphic plate instead of glass, so the numbers read as pressed into a panel.
              A brass rule sits between number and label, like a spec plate's own divider.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">C — Ridge tab, bento</p>
            <div class="stage stage-stats">
              <ul class="stats-c">
                <li class="glass stat-c stat-c-lead">
                  <span class="stat-c-tab">01</span>
                  <span class="stat-value">3</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Node versions in the field</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat-c">
                  <span class="stat-c-tab">02</span>
                  <span class="stat-value">30 s</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">To cancel a false fall alarm</span>
                </li>
                <li class="glass stat-c">
                  <span class="stat-c-tab">03</span>
                  <span class="stat-value">0</span>
                  <span class="stat-label">Cell towers required</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <p class="rev-note">
              An asymmetric lead card at double width for the number the page most wants
              read first, a small brass index tab on every card. Closer to the Codespot
              reference's big-numeral bento, in this page's own geometry.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <!-- 5. GRAIN AND CONTOURS -->
      <!-- ============================================================ -->
      <section class="rev-section" id="rev-texture">
        <h2>5. Wood grain and contour lines</h2>
        <p class="rev-intro">
          Both textures sit behind a glass panel so it has something to refract. Judging
          whether they earn their place at three strengths: shipped, half, gone.
        </p>

        <h3 class="rev-sub">Wood grain, behind the hero glass</h3>
        <div class="rev-grid rev-grid-3">
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">A — Shipped, 0.55 opacity</p>
            <div class="stage stage-texture grain-a">
              <div class="glass texture-card above">
                <span class="stat-value">v4</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Current node</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">B — Half, 0.28 opacity</p>
            <div class="stage stage-texture grain-b">
              <div class="glass texture-card above">
                <span class="stat-value">v4</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Current node</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">C — Removed</p>
            <div class="stage stage-texture">
              <div class="glass texture-card above">
                <span class="stat-value">v4</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Current node</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="rev-sub">Topographic contours, behind the research glass</h3>
        <div class="rev-grid rev-grid-3">
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">A — Shipped, 0.3 opacity</p>
            <div class="stage stage-texture contours-a">
              <div class="glass texture-card above">
                <span class="stat-value">01</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Nothing is lost while the link is down</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">B — Half, 0.16 opacity</p>
            <div class="stage stage-texture contours-b">
              <div class="glass texture-card above">
                <span class="stat-value">01</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Nothing is lost while the link is down</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rev-card">
            <p class="rev-label">C — Removed</p>
            <div class="stage stage-texture">
              <div class="glass texture-card above">
                <span class="stat-value">01</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Nothing is lost while the link is down</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .rev-shell {
    max-width: var(--shell);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--section-y) var(--gutter) 8rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 4.5rem;
  }

  .rev-banner {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .rev-banner h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }
  .rev-jump {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.2rem;
  }
  .rev-jump a {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--moss);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--moss-deep);
  }
  .rev-jump a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .rev-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--surface-ridge);
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .rev-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
  .rev-sub {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .rev-intro {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .rev-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .rev-grid-2 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
  .rev-grid-3 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .rev-grid-3 {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .rev-grid-2 {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .rev-card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .rev-label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brass);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .rev-note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* --- shared stage shell ------------------------------------------- */
  .stage {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface-base);
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-ridge);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  /* --- 1. hero glow stages ------------------------------------------- */
  .stage-hero {
    padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
    min-height: 20rem;
    display: grid;
    align-content: center;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stage-hero-content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    justify-items: center;
  }
  .stage-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .stage-h1 .accent {
    color: var(--moss);
  }
  .badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.9rem 0.35rem 0.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-edge);
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 4%);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .badge-chip {
    background: var(--brass);
    color: var(--ink-inverse);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .glow-a {
    position: absolute;
    top: -16rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 46rem;
    height: 26rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      rgb(192 138 62 / 22%) 0%,
      rgb(143 175 116 / 9%) 38%,
      transparent 68%
    );
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .glow-b-core {
    position: absolute;
    top: -6rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 20rem;
    height: 16rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      rgb(192 138 62 / 42%) 0%,
      rgb(232 196 138 / 16%) 40%,
      transparent 72%
    );
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .glow-b-vignette {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      transparent 45%,
      rgb(13 17 11 / 55%) 100%
    );
  }

  .glow-c-beam {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 16rem;
    height: 34rem;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      rgb(232 196 138 / 30%) 0%,
      rgb(192 138 62 / 12%) 45%,
      transparent 85%
    );
    clip-path: polygon(38% 0%, 62% 0%, 100% 100%, 0% 100%);
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .glow-c-core {
    position: absolute;
    top: -4rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 14rem;
    height: 10rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      rgb(143 175 116 / 30%) 0%,
      transparent 70%
    );
    z-index: 0;
  }

  /* --- 2. mobile frames ------------------------------------------------ */
  .phone-frame {
    width: 375px;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    background: var(--surface-base);
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-ridge);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .m-stats {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }
  .m-stats-a {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  .m-stats-a .stat {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .m-stats-b {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  }
  .m-stats-b .stat-lead {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .m-stats .stat {
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
  }
  .m-stats .stat-value {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    color: var(--brass);
    display: block;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .m-stats .stat-label {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }
  .m-stats-b .stat:not(.stat-lead) .stat-value {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .m-chips {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .m-chips-a {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .m-chips-a li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-ridge);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .m-chips-b-wrap {
    margin-inline: -1rem;
    padding-inline: 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0,
      black 1.2rem,
      black calc(100% - 1.2rem),
      transparent 100%
    );
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0,
      black 1.2rem,
      black calc(100% - 1.2rem),
      transparent 100%
    );
  }
  .m-chips-b {
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
  }
  .m-chips-b li {
    flex: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-ridge);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
